suid,nodev via persistent /etc/fstab tmpfs entries, verified enforcement functionally before and after a full reboot, and confirmed the node's boot identity changed (restart proof) with settings surviving.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected baseline mount/fstab state on node1 (Alpine 3.23.3)\",\"Backed up /etc/fstab and appended tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,relatime\",\"Applied immediately via `mount /tmp` and `mount -o remount /dev/shm`\",\"Functionally verified noexec (script execution denied), nosuid (setuid busybox binary execution denied), and nodev (device node open denied) on both mounts\",\"Captured pre-reboot boot_id baseline\",\"Triggered a native reboot via backgrounded `reboot` so the ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned\",\"Confirmed new boot_id differs from baseline, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified /etc/fstab and live mount options for /tmp and /dev/shm post-reboot\",\"Re-ran the noexec/nosuid/nodev functional checks post-reboot to confirm persistence\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline mount/fstab state before changes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dc7db08cdec14666\",\"cmd-9a00c9985ef242ff\",\"cmd-ec5e144b07fa42a5\"],\"summary\":\"Showed /dev/shm already tmpfs but with no fstab entry, and /tmp was not a separate mount at all; neither had fstab entries.\"},{\"requirement\":\"fstab updated with persistent noexec,nosuid,nodev options for /tmp and /dev/shm\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cc6932c629c7439b\"],\"summary\":\"Backed up fstab and appended tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,relatime.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mount options applied live and match fstab\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-50d12e707873458d\"],\"summary\":\"mount /tmp and remount of /dev/shm show both as tmpfs with nosuid,nodev,noexec.\"},{\"requirement\":\"noexec, nosuid, nodev functionally enforced pre-reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-58a25c08420b4986\",\"cmd-a977ad90d80149f3\",\"cmd-86b50fdebb244eb4\"],\"summary\":\"Script execution from /tmp denied (exit 126), setuid busybox execution from /dev/shm denied (exit 126), and opening a device node created in /tmp denied (Permission denied) despite mknod itself succeeding.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline boot identity captured before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f39b3a354ef74c9c\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id f3e63865-c712-4b78-90cd-97c193bd1d83 and confirmed both mounts healthy just before reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3ae82af7364741e8\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded `reboot` command acknowledged (reboot_scheduled) and returned before the node disconnected on the next call.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e388e06de98f4003\",\"cmd-e5000c6477864079\",\"cmd-2c6be83f7e3c4f0d\",\"cmd-a4dbea2b2a354d1a\",\"cmd-a74ed43dcd7e4844\",\"cmd-cc8ab7533051449c\",\"cmd-825737f5a9b14da1\"],\"summary\":\"Node was unreachable through several poll attempts (connection reset/timeout) during reboot, then exec availability returned with a new boot_id ca0d1bc4-614c-475a-b0b7-f7947d397461 (differs from baseline) and uptime of 0 minutes, proving an actual restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mount hardening persisted across reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a6e7db4b5fd14284\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot mount and fstab output show /tmp and /dev/shm both mounted tmpfs with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec, matching the fstab entries added earlier.\"},{\"requirement\":\"noexec, nosuid, nodev functionally enforced post-reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1f56d41260724033\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot: script execution from /tmp denied, setuid busybox execution from /dev/shm denied, and device node access from /tmp denied — confirming the hardening is active and persistent after restart.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Hardened /tmp and /dev/shm on node1 with noe